    "result": "## \u2705 Feature Implementation Complete\n\nI've successfully implemented the one-line summary feature for frai-gate CI logs. Here's what was added:\n\n### 1. **`renderSummary()` function** (src/gate/report.ts)\n- Returns format: `<VERDICT> <answered>/<total>` where total = 7 (all GATE_CHECKS)\n- `answered` = checks with no block-severity findings (warnings don't reduce it)\n- Appends blocked check IDs in GATE_CHECKS order when blocks exist\n- Special case: returns `BLOCK 0/7: structure` if gate section is missing\n- Example outputs:\n  - `PASS 7/7` (all checks answered)\n  - `WARN 7/7` (only warnings, no blocks)\n  - `BLOCK 5/7: risk-tier, evaluation` (2 checks blocked)\n\n### 2. **`--summary` flag** to `frai-gate check`\n- Prints only the summary line instead of full report\n- Exit codes unchanged (1 on BLOCK, 0 on PASS/WARN)\n- `--json` takes priority if both flags provided\n- Updated HELP text and usage message\n\n### 3. **Tests** (src/gate/report.test.ts)\n- 9 comprehensive test cases covering all scenarios\n- All 20 tests passing \u2713\n\n### 4. **Verification**\n- \u2705 Build successful (`pnpm --filter frai-gate build`)\n- \u2705 All tests passing (`pnpm --filter frai-gate test`)\n- \u2705 CLI works with `--summary` flag\n- \u2705 `--json` takes priority over `--summary`\n- \u2705 Function exported from public API",
